{"i": 55, "key": "ig2b02:p6:scorpio:counter", "label": "Scorpio sample counter", "kind": "diagram", "box": [71895, 791666, 134804, 840278], "components": ["Scorpio", "1 identifier", "LI", "1 red/yellow rating", "2", "3", "Artillery illustration"], "uncertainty": ["Small counter glyphs are literal observations; exact transcription and semantic interpretation remain pending."], "text": ""}
{"i": 56, "key": "ig2b02:p6:scorpio:text-b", "label": "Scorpio (below counter)", "kind": "clause", "box": [71895, 849116, 487746, 880051], "components": ["Continued prose"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "was used almost entirely for camp defense (the size, range and use\nof these early artillery pieces is open to much debate)."}
{"i": 57, "key": "ig2b02:p6:scale-heading", "label": "2.5 GAME SCALE", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 66287, 928922, 85228], "components": ["2.5 GAME SCALE"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "2.5 GAME SCALE"}
{"i": 58, "key": "ig2b02:p6:scale-hex-turn", "label": "Hex distance and game-turn time", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 85858, 928922, 117425], "components": ["Hex distance and game-turn time"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Each hex is approximately 70+ paces (yards) from side to side.\nEach game turn covers about 20 minutes of real time."}
{"i": 59, "key": "ig2b02:p6:scale-size", "label": "Size scale and skirmisher exception", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 123106, 928922, 275884], "components": ["Size scale and skirmisher exception"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Each point of Size denotes from 100-150 infantry (depending on\ntheir formation, rank depth and usage) or 100 cavalry. Thus, an\nAfrican Phalanx unit represents 1500+ men, a Roman Principes\nunit 300, and a Roman Heavy Cavalry unit about 300 men. Each\nRoman legion infantry unit is the equivalent of 2\u20133 maniples\n(granted, that\u2019s an unwieldy division of labor; however, it makes\nfrontages realistic and, more importantly, the game playable).\nSkirmishers are an exception; their size reflects not their numeri-\ncal strength but their dispersed type of formation. Size, players\nwill soon realize, is the least important rating a unit has."}
{"i": 60, "key": "ig2b02:p6:scale-frontage", "label": "Counter shape and frontage", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 281565, 928922, 343435], "components": ["Counter shape and frontage"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "The counter shape of a unit represents its frontage. A Phalanx\nin full array had a frontage of approximately 150 yards; thus,\nit occupies 2 hexes. A cavalry unit had a frontage of about 50+\nyards, or one hex."}
{"i": 61, "key": "ig2b02:p6:length-heading", "label": "2.6 GAME LENGTH", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 352904, 928922, 371844], "components": ["2.6 GAME LENGTH"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "2.6 GAME LENGTH"}
{"i": 62, "key": "ig2b02:p6:length-withdrawal", "label": "Battle duration and withdrawal", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 372474, 928922, 404041], "components": ["Battle duration and withdrawal"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Generally, battles are fought until one side withdraws, so there\nis usually no need to keep track of how many turns have passed."}
{"i": 63, "key": "ig2b02:p6:length-turn-track", "label": "Game Turn Track", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 409722, 928922, 456440], "components": ["Game Turn Track"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "A Game Turn Track has been provided to help track the timing\nof certain events (the entry of reinforcements, etc.) in some of\nthe battles."}
{"i": 64, "key": "ig2b02:p6:length-historical-note", "label": "Historical note on duration and casualties", "kind": "note", "box": [513071, 458964, 928922, 571970], "components": ["Historical note on duration and casualties"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "HISTORICAL NOTE: Roman battles took somewhat longer\nto complete than those of just 150 or so years previously.\nParticipants had developed a wide variety of tactical sys-\ntems to counter those of their enemy. In addition, armor and\nprotection were lighter and more efficient, enabling soldiers\nto fight longer. The result of all this was that casualties rose\nprecipitously, and battles lasted a great deal longer."}
{"i": 65, "key": "ig2b02:p6:latin-heading", "label": "2.7 LATIN", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 585858, 928922, 605430], "components": ["2.7 LATIN"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "2.7 LATIN"}
{"i": 66, "key": "ig2b02:p6:latin-prose", "label": "Editorial Latin terminology discussion", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 606060, 928922, 682450], "components": ["Editorial Latin terminology discussion"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "We have tried to use appropriate Latin military terms, as appli-\ncable. Six years of hacking one\u2019s way through Caesar\u2019s Com-\nmentaries finally came to some use. Memory, however, is a great\nvillain. I think we got most of the \u201cendings\u201d right; then again, if\nit came from the fifth declension, we probably \u201cbluu\u201d it."}
{"i": 67, "key": "ig2b02:p6:sequence-heading", "label": "3.0 SEQUENCE OF PLAY", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 700757, 928922, 727273], "components": ["3.0 SEQUENCE OF PLAY"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "3.0 SEQUENCE OF PLAY"}
{"i": 68, "key": "ig2b02:p6:sequence-introduction", "label": "Sequence of Play introduction", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 727904, 928922, 804925], "components": ["Sequence of Play introduction"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "Players activate each of their leaders in the order determined by\ntheir Initiative Rating. When a leader is activated, he issues orders\nwhich enable units to move and conduct combat. After all leaders\nare Finished, play proceeds to the Rout and Reload Phase, after\nwhich each player checks to see if his army withdraws."}
{"i": 69, "key": "ig2b02:p6:activation-heading", "label": "A. Leader Activation Phase", "kind": "heading", "box": [513071, 813762, 928922, 832703], "components": ["A. Leader Activation Phase"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "A. Leader Activation Phase"}
{"i": 70, "key": "ig2b02:p6:activation-prose", "label": "Leader Activation Phase paragraph", "kind": "clause", "box": [513071, 833964, 928922, 910985], "components": ["Leader Activation Phase paragraph"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "The player with the lowest Initiative-rated leader who has not yet\nbeen activated activates that leader. If a DR is required to enable\nthe activated leader to issue a Line Command, he rolls for such\nability at this point (4.33). Non-Momentum Trump attempts may\nbe made at this time (5.41)."}
{"i": 71, "key": "ig2b02:p6:copyright-footer", "label": "Copyright footer", "kind": "editorial", "box": [426470, 945707, 573530, 960228], "components": ["Copyright symbol", "2026 GMT Games, LLC"], "uncertainty": [], "text": "\u00a9 2026 GMT Games, LLC"}

